cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >
  If you use this code or build on this research, please cite the
  following work. The paper is currently under review.
title: >
  Markov Logic Process: Augmenting Reinforcement Learning with
  Symbolic Association-Rule Reasoning via the Logos Module
authors:
  - family-names: Jain
    given-names: Saiyam
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"   # replace with real ORCID
  - family-names: Bhowmik
    given-names: Swaroop
  - family-names: Choudhury
    given-names: Dipanjan
  - family-names: Sahoo
    given-names: Santosh Kumar
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2025-01-01"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/saiyamjain/markov-logic-process"
url: "https://github.com/saiyamjain/markov-logic-process"
abstract: >
  We propose the Markov Logic Process (MLP), a six-tuple
  (S, A, P, R, γ, L) that extends the classical MDP with a Logos
  module capable of online symbolic association-rule discovery.
  The Logos-augmented Bellman operator V_L(s) = max_a[R(s,a) +
  λΦ_L(s,a) + γV_L(s')] shapes both the value update and action
  selection using logic potentials mined asynchronously from the
  agent's own experience replay buffer. Ablation studies on
  LunarLander (standard and wind/turbulence variants) over 5 seeds
  show MLP-Full achieves +21.7% and +31.4% improvements over the
  DQN baseline, with significantly improved post-convergence
  stability and reduced catastrophic failure modes.
keywords:
  - reinforcement-learning
  - Markov-decision-process
  - association-rule-mining
  - symbolic-reasoning
  - deep-Q-network
  - reward-shaping
  - neuro-symbolic-AI
  - LunarLander
